Original conformance source section Company-specific augmentation:
The source already maps web/mobile/document/design-system/CI accessibility checks, visual/DOM/keyboard/ARIA/contrast/forms/media, human review, remediation/regression, evidence, private runners, Brain/agents/services and explicit automated-vs-human coverage. Current-standard completion adds:

- lifecycle: authorized target → baseline → deterministic automated checks → clustered findings → required human-review queue → remediation → CI/rescan → verified closure → regression monitoring → evidence/report/export/offboard;
- support/operations for dynamic content, shadow DOM, canvas/custom widgets, auth flows, RTL/localization, screen-reader semantics, mobile differences and PDF reading order;
- legal/truth boundary: technical evidence never equals legal certification; jurisdiction-specific interpretation remains specialist/human;
- abuse/security controls for unauthorized scanning, credential leakage, captured PII/source leakage, fabricated pass evidence and waiver misuse;
- observability/incidents across evaluator/rule versions, coverage, false positives/negatives, manual-review backlog, regression rate, runner health and artifact integrity; incident response can quarantine evaluator versions and mark affected results unknown;
- testing/evals on representative assistive-tech/user-need scenarios, keyboard/focus, semantics, contrast, forms, captions, PDF/mobile and deliberate evaluator blind spots;
- shadow/canary evaluator deployment, deterministic versioned evidence, rollback, performance/cost per page/screen/component/doc/CI run;
- financial truth, global standards/jurisdiction packs, accessibility of the product itself, mobile review, optional voice, multimodal evidence;
- training/expert-review coordination, controlled rule experiments, evaluator/target/CI-gate safe mode and portable evidence export;
- reuse candidates: testing/evaluation factory, browser/device runners, artifact/evidence, rule/version registry, CI gates and human-review state. Shared evaluator defects can produce false assurance across products, requiring canary/version isolation.

Original conformance source section Company-specific augmentation:
The source already maps return taxonomy, defect/sizing/expectation/fulfillment/supplier/fraud signals, cost/disposition, root-cause/forecast, catalog fixes, supplier feedback, policy analytics, Brain/agents/services and protected refund policy. Current-standard completion adds:

- lifecycle: authorized return/order events → reason/evidence normalization → order/SKU/variant/catalog/supplier/fulfillment version linkage → multi-cause classification → cost/risk/root-cause → recommended fix → authorized source-system change → future-return outcome measurement → attribution/export/offboard;
- support/operations for bad reason codes, remorse vs defect, product-version changes, unknown supplier lots, counterfeit/carrier damage, seasonality and policy-change confounding;
- privacy/legal/abuse: minimize customer/order/media PII, uncertain fraud labels, no discriminatory/refund decisions, evidence-backed supplier claims, defend against return/fraud-data poisoning and unsupported customer penalties;
- observability/incidents for reason quality, linkage completeness, fraud confidence/calibration, product/supplier recurrence, cost/disposition, catalog version, fix experiments and outcome attribution; pause affected recommendations/refund-related automation and retract unsupported labels;
- testing/evals across vertical taxonomies, multi-cause returns, sparse batches, image/text evidence, fraud false positives and causal confounding;
- shadow/canary classifiers/models, rollback, performance/cost and verified financial-value metrics only;
- locale/language/size/unit/product taxonomy support, accessibility, mobile review, optional voice, multimodal photo/video evidence with privacy/provenance;
- training, experiments/holdouts, product/supplier/model safe modes, export/portability;
- reuse candidates: commerce event model, product/catalog/supplier provenance, media/document pipeline, fraud/evals, experiment/attribution and financial action gates. Shared product/fraud/refund defects can create customer/supplier harm and require strict scoping/versioning.

Original conformance source section Company-specific augmentation:
The source already maps claim intake, product/serial/ownership, exact coverage version, multimodal evidence, fraud/anomaly, repair/replacement/reimbursement support, service routing, approvals, portals/status, reserves, appeals, Brain/agents/services and protected material decisions. Current-standard completion adds:

- lifecycle: claim → identity/product/purchase verification → exact policy/version → evidence quality/classification → deterministic eligibility → fraud/anomaly → cost/resolution options → required approval → separately authorized fulfillment → resolution verification → appeal/product-quality feedback → export/offboard;
- support/operations for gifts/secondhand ownership, missing receipts, serial/counterfeit issues, intermittent defects, ambiguous media, prior repairs, shipping-vs-manufacturer cause, recalls, duplicate claims and stock shortages;
- security/privacy/legal: claimant PII/financial/media protection, no unsupported fraud accusations, jurisdiction/insurance separation, appeal rights and protected denial/payment/refund/replacement/repair actions;
- abuse controls for forged purchase/evidence, duplicate claims, serial manipulation, collusion and attempts to force favorable eligibility;
- observability/incidents for identity/serial/purchase confidence, policy version, evidence completeness, eligibility result, fraud calibration, approval/SLA, inventory/provider fulfillment and appeal state; freeze material actions and revert affected rule/model versions on defect;
- tests/evals for coverage supersession, evidence ambiguity, safety recall, fraud false positives, appeals, provider/inventory failures and deterministic policy ownership;
- shadow/canary rule/model/vision versions, rollback, performance/cost per claim/media/OCR/model/provider; verified commercial/claims savings only from real evidence;
- localization/accessibility/mobile/voice/multimodal, operator training, controlled experiments, per-policy/model/action safe mode and portable claim/evidence/history export;
- reuse candidates: workflow/state machine, policy/version registry, identity/product registry, secure document/media, fraud/evals, approval/action gates, provider routing and audit. Shared eligibility/policy/fraud defects have critical customer/legal/financial blast radius.
